 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** The merge process is $O(N \log K)$, where $N$ is the total number of splats and $K$ is the number of active renderers, as it performs a binary merge tree of depth $K$ [S1, unofficial]. Each merge step is linear in the number of elements being merged.
-- **Memory Complexity:** Requires four scratch buffers of size $N$ and one output buffer of size $N$, totaling $5N$ elements (orders and depths) [S1, unofficial].
-- **Performance:** Relies on GPU hardware acceleration, specifically requiring wave/subgroup operations available in D3D12, Metal, or Vulkan [S1, unofficial]. WebGPU supports subgroups but may not be implemented in all engines (e.g., Unity) [S1, unofficial].
+- **Time Complexity:** The merge process is $O(NK)$, where $N$ is the total number of splats and $K$ is the number of active renderers, as it performs an iterative pairwise merge across $K-1$ stages [S1, unofficial]. Each merge step is linear in the number of elements being merged [S1, unofficial].
+- **Memory Complexity:** Requires four scratch buffers and one output buffer, each of size $N$, totaling $5N$ elements for orders and depths [S1, unofficial].
+- **Performance:** Relies on GPU hardware acceleration, specifically requiring wave/subgroup operations available in D3D12, Metal, or Vulkan [S1, unofficial]. WebGPU supports subgroups but may lack engine implementation (e.g., Unity) [S1, unofficial].
 - **Strengths:** Reduces overdraw and improves sorting accuracy across scenes by merging multiple renderers into a single globally depth-sorted draw call [S1, unofficial].
-- **Limitations:** Requires specific graphics APIs (no OpenGL/WebGL support due to subgroup requirements) [S1, unofficial]. Fallback to per-renderer sorting if uncompressed assets are present [S1, unofficial].
-- **When to use:** When rendering multiple independent Gaussian Splat scenes in a unified view with correct depth compositing.
-- **When not to use:** When only a single renderer is active, or when uncompressed assets are used and global sorting is required.
